{"is_source_file": true, "format": "JavaScript (React JSX)", "description": "This file is the main React component for a simple web-based drawing application. It manages the drawing canvas, tools (brush and eraser), color palette, brush sizes, undo/redo history, and saving the drawing as a PNG image. The component handles user input via pointer events, dynamically resizes the canvas, and maintains internal state for the drawing tools and history.", "external_files": ["./App.css"], "external_methods": ["window.devicePixelRatio", "window.addEventListener", "window.removeEventListener", "document.createElement", "document.body.appendChild", "document.body.removeChild", "canvas.getContext", "canvas.toDataURL"], "published": ["App"], "classes": [], "methods": [{"name": "syncHistoryMeta", "description": "Updates the undo/redo availability state based on the current history stack and index."}, {"name": "get2DContext", "description": "Retrieves the 2D rendering context of the canvas with 'willReadFrequently' set to true."}, {"name": "getCanvasCssSize", "description": "Returns the current size of the canvas in CSS pixels."}, {"name": "fillWhiteBackground", "description": "Fills the entire canvas with a white background, handling device pixel ratio scaling."}, {"name": "captureSnapshot", "description": "Captures the current canvas content as an ImageData snapshot and manages the undo history stack."}, {"name": "applySnapshot", "description": "Restores a given ImageData snapshot onto the canvas."}, {"name": "undo", "description": "Reverts the canvas to the previous snapshot in the undo history."}, {"name": "redo", "description": "Reapplies the next snapshot in the undo history, if available."}, {"name": "setCanvasSizeToContainer", "description": "Resizes the canvas to match the container's dimensions, maintaining aspect ratio and preserving current drawing."}, {"name": "getPointFromEvent", "description": "Converts a pointer event to canvas coordinates based on the bounding rec